* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Index artifacts: never touch their bytes. vectors.npy is a raw float32 buffer, and
# chunks.jsonl is read by byte offset in places — CRLF conversion on either would corrupt
# the index silently, which is the worst way for it to break.
#
# These patterns are version-agnostic on purpose. They used to name V9.0 explicitly, which
# meant the moment the deployment moved to V10.0 its index fell back to `text=auto` and was
# protected only by git's binary sniffing rather than by a declared rule. Sniffing got it
# right, but a rule that silently stops applying when a folder is renamed is not a rule.
**/index_store/vectors.npy binary
**/index_store/*.jsonl -text
**/index_store/*.json -text
*.woff2 binary
*.wav binary
